## Behavioral rules (Karpathy-inspired)
<!-- Distilled from https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills/blob/main/CLAUDE.md -->
- Think before coding: state assumptions, surface tradeoffs, ask when unclear — never silently pick an interpretation.
- Simplicity first: minimum code that solves the problem; no speculative features, single-use abstractions, or impossible-scenario handling.
- Surgical changes: touch only what the task requires; match existing style; mention unrelated dead code, don't delete it; clean up only orphans your changes created.
- Goal-driven: turn tasks into verifiable goals (test first, then implement); loop until verified.
- Wrong/right examples per principle: `coding-discipline` skill.

